<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>India: Delhi chokes on most polluted Diwali eve in 10 years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bde8502d9efb3362ab6d60bf98429da5bf9187794fb64bc81a48ef88656bcedd</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T07:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-delhi-chokes-on-most-polluted-diwali-eve-in-10-years/live-79883248--b4ed1b7f6c06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-delhi-chokes-on-most-polluted-diwali-eve-in-10-years/live-79883248?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Delhi was ranked as the world's most polluted major city on the eve of Diwali. Delhi's air pollution is expected to get worse in the coming days.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US asks China to uphold Busan trade deal commitments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a5a4031915a5ab234ee1c01ec43197e6a8d331f0b05fa1372628d6014b6091d</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T04:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-asks-china-to-uphold-busan-trade-deal-commitments/a-79882939--7107d3b9b548.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-asks-china-to-uphold-busan-trade-deal-commitments/a-79882939?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US urged Beijing to meet commitments from a 2025 accord — particularly on agricultural purchases and rare earths supply. China, meanwhile, expressed concern over the US' "economic, trade restrictive" measures.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>For people in Iran, a constant threat of war and dearth of information</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56d72413df66e071600cec0eea962d6291bbeeb3d2e943e7f8fb2263558e6013</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/for-people-in-iran-a-constant-threat-of-war-and-dearth-of-information/a-79875438--15c623b3dc73.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/for-people-in-iran-a-constant-threat-of-war-and-dearth-of-information/a-79875438?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Most people in Iran have little idea of the course of the US-led war and peace talks on the global stage. With few sources of information, the population must navigate conflicting rumors and fears of a nuclear attack.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>'No choice but to bear it': Delhi's unrelenting air pollution crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13585655ca57fd0a73bc41af6a3cb21b46e7bd0376c12a288b6df7fbb5a73b2c</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T12:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124--aa42da1e16d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/no-choice-but-to-bear-it-delhi-s-unrelenting-air-pollution-crisis/a-79873124?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite years of government interventions, emergency restrictions and public outrage, Delhi continues to battle dangerously polluted air every winter. Why isn't there a lasting solution to a predictable crisis?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran signals satisfaction, skepticism after US midterm vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:acf2be4288e34c6daed4513df1604169c5d33ce554783e3899963340e684e9ee</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149--f14e22022dc8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-signals-satisfaction-skepticism-after-us-midterm-vote/a-79867149?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the Iranian regime says the US midterms will not change Washington's policy toward Tehran, some officials and commentators see the resounding Democratic victory as blowback against the Iran war.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What does Trump's midterm elections loss mean for strained US-India ties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:13aaf55797ec72c1e56bbb94eb79e21a9452a69dc618fb3a998668d9f784f750</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T13:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-does-trump-s-midterm-elections-loss-mean-for-strained-us-india-ties/a-79865777--7836c1679b1c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-does-trump-s-midterm-elections-loss-mean-for-strained-us-india-ties/a-79865777?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's electoral setback might give New Delhi and Washington space to reset relations, but there is no guarantee that the US will actually change its approach to India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea tests Arctic shipping route amid Russia-West row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e02cc59e70ebebd98bbea286f5220e6bfcd25278e40bf5bf3d48cc22e763eda</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907--d831b46c670a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-tests-arctic-shipping-route-amid-russia-west-row/a-79853907?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For South Korean ships, navigating off the north coast of Russia dramatically reduces travel time to Europe, but the pro-Ukraine coalition might see it as undermining their efforts to isolate Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>8 ways the US midterm election could affect Donald Trump's Iran policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a32e88a8b9031df3fcd76a56a87501df645c286f38c6d0c75aa425b089fa4bb4</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-02T15:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/8-ways-the-us-midterm-election-could-affect-donald-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79831816--8cf7f9243f7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/8-ways-the-us-midterm-election-could-affect-donald-trump-s-iran-policy/a-79831816?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While the US midterms could open a window for diplomacy with Iran, they could also unleash a new military escalation. DW spoke with analysts to identify eight factors that could tip the balance toward war or peace.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02c897b1188dc56aa7635610b875c9a6ec585de865ac3bece95dbfaf201a41db</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is Iran headed to war or peace after Mecca alliance meeting?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a3279be22e5c6655d8f26cb67f0f70830893102ef42aad04dae0645476771f4</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-28T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256--9ef674df50a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-iran-headed-to-war-or-peace-after-mecca-alliance-meeting/a-79788256?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia, Pakistan and Turkey have taken their latest peace push directly to Tehran. Officially, it was to avert a new military escalation, but their diplomatic outreach can also be seen as a warning to Iran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Will elections in Israel change its Iran approach?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e62592511b46894eb26c331111da9f059d08e18d792f188df6932faa2edbf0f</id><updated>2026-11-08T20:38:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T13:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122--d46c291154a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-elections-in-israel-change-its-iran-approach/a-79776122?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls, the country's conflict with Iran casts a long shadow over the ballot box. But any leadership changes in Israel may not be enough to shake up its grand strategy on Tehran.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
